dry Software,https://nutjs.dev/,2026-11-21,nutjs.dev,2021-08-25,62,0,2026-08-10,1,Inc,0,1,0,1,0,,,,3,210,,,,,,,"nut.js Docs Plugins Examples AI Agents Pricing Blog Changelog Search docs... ⌘K Cross-platform desktop automation Automate your desktop with Node.js The powerful, intuitive library for desktop automation, E2E testing, and building intelligent desktop agents. Control mouse, keyboard, and screen across Windows, macOS, and Linux. Get Started View on GitHub Prebuilt binaries No build tools needed automation.ts Copy import { mouse, Button, keyboard, straightTo, centerOf, getActiveWindow } from ""@nut-tree/nut-js"" ; import { useElementInspector } from ""@nut-tree/element-inspector"" ; import { elements } from ""@nut-tree/element-inspector/win"" ; useElementInspector (); // Get the active window const window = await getActiveWindow (); // Find a button by its label and click it const submitBtn = await window. find ( elements. button ({ title: ""Submit"" }) ); await mouse. move ( straightTo ( centerOf (submitBtn.region))); await mouse. click (Button. LEFT ); // Type text with natural speed await keyboard. type ( ""Hello, nut.js!"" ); Trusted by developers and teams worldwide working on Windows , macOS or Linux Everything you need for desktop automation nut.js provides a comprehensive toolkit for controlling desktop applications programmatically with an intuitive, promise-based API. Mouse Control Precise mouse movements, clicks, drags, and scrolling with configurable speed and easing functions. Keyboard Input Type text, press key combinations, and simulate any keyboard interaction with ease. S"
HabitKit,https://habitkit.app/,2026-11-21,habitkit.app,2021-08-15,63,0,2026-10-27,0,,0,0,0,1,0,,,,1,2,,,,,,,"Habit Kit Features Reviews Guides Get the app Features Reviews Guides The habit tracker you can actually see One tap logs the day. Every day fills a tile, and the grid becomes a chain you won't want to break. Free on iPhone and Android, private, no account needed. Also on the App Store Also on Google Play Point your phone camera at the code to open HabitKit in the store. Close TRUSTED BY 500,000+ HABIT BUILDERS AS FEATURED IN The Studio Starter Story One tap a day . Workouts, pages read, glasses of water, days without a cigarette. If it happens on a day, it gets a tile. Setting one up takes three steps. 1 Name it, colour it Tap the plus button, type a name, pick the colour its tiles will fill with. Save. There is nothing else to fill in, and nobody to sign up as first. 2 Tap once when you do it One tap on the card logs today, a second clears it again. Forgot Tuesday? Open the habit and fill it in from its calendar. A late tick counts exactly as much as a punctual one. 3 Watch the year fill in One tile a day, one column a week, a year-long heatmap with today at the right-hand edge. Some mornings that grid is the only argument you need. No account, no feed, nobody to be compared against. Reminders exist only if you ask for one, and a day you miss is an empty square. That is the whole punishment. Have a look inside . Real screens from the iPhone and Android app. Nothing here is a mockup. Home screen widgets Grids and streaks on your home screen. Check off without opening the app"
